{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #890: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. If $\\omega(n)$ counts the number of distinct prime factors of $n$, then is it true that, for every $k\\geq 1$,\\[\\liminf_{n\\to \\infty}\\sum_{0\\leq i<k}\\omega(n+i)\\leq k+\\pi(k)?\\]Is it true that\\[\\limsup_{n\\to \\infty}\\left(\\sum_{0\\leq i<k}\\omega(n+i)\\right) \\frac{\\log\\log n}{\\log n}=1?\\] Current best: A question of Erd\\H{o}s and Selfridge \\cite{ErSe67}, who observe that\\[\\liminf_{n\\to \\infty}\\sum_{0\\leq i<k}\\omega(n+i)\\geq k+\\pi(k)-1\\]for every $k$. Prize: no. Tags: number theory, primes."},"claim_id":"vcl_86d73f178f93aa49f26e0332bf7b14a00e285351f4f67a98455dda19166529ff","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:890","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_16d3ac5a3c7bb62c","object_root":"sha256:195385d540eb0734835737d154a78c5840d258d1d2370a69938a7c63a00db136","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:890"}],